From: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:07:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/11] arm64: dts: komodo: enable syscon-reboot-mode

zumapro.dtsi already describes the reboot-mode child of the PMU
(syscon-reboot-mode, offset 0x810 = SYSIP_DAT0, mode-normal 0x00,
mode-bootloader 0xfc) but leaves it disabled; the tegu and comet boards
enable it, komodo did not, so /sys/class/reboot-mode was missing and
"reboot bootloader" only rebooted slot B.

CONFIG_REBOOT_MODE=y and CONFIG_SYSCON_REBOOT_MODE=y are already set and
the PMU (google,zuma-pmu, SMC-backed regmap registered as syscon) is
already enabled on komodo. On zuma, a cold PSCI SYSTEM_RESET clears
SYSIP_DAT0, so this needs reboot=warm on the command line (PSCI 1.1
SYSTEM_RESET2), added by device-google-komodo.

Tested on komodo, with reboot=warm.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
index 1eb1d38e1..23ade1182 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
@@ -175,6 +175,17 @@ &pmu_system_controller {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * Reboot reason for the bootloader: SYSIP_DAT0 (PMU + 0x810), 0xfc =
+ * bootloader (fastboot), 0x00 = normal, as on zuma husky/akita and zumapro
+ * tegu/comet. A cold PSCI reset clears the register before ABL reads it,
+ * so "reboot bootloader" also needs reboot=warm (PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2) on
+ * the command line; the device package adds it.
+ */
+&reboot_mode {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /* The watchdog clocks are supplied by these disabled-by-default CMUs. */
 &cmu_top {
 	status = "okay";
